{"url": "https://www.engr.pitt.edu/graduate/graduate-admissions/graduate-application", "final_url": "https://www.engineering.pitt.edu/academics/graduateadmissions/graduate-applications/", "status": 200, "method": "http", "fetched": "2026-10-24", "text": "Graduate Applications\nSkip to main content\nSwanson School of Engineering\nOpen Navigation\nOpen configuration options\nConfigure block\nRemove block\nEdit view\nOpen configuration options\nEdit view\nGraduate Application\nThank you for your interest in the Swanson School of Engineering\u2019s graduate programs! Ready to apply? Select your intended start term below. Pitt students participating in Pitt2Pitt or EAGr should NOT select a regular application term - Please see the special instructions below.\nSpring 2027, Fall 2027 & Spring 2028\nStart your application today and save your progress as you go. Be sure to review the deadlines for each term here. Please note that Pitt2Pitt and EAGr applicants should NOT apply using this link. We can\u2019t wait to see your application\u2014let\u2019s get started!\nSpring 2027 Application\nFall 2027 & Spring 2028 Application\nPitt2Pitt or EAGr\nTo apply to Pitt2Pitt or EAGr, please email SSOE Graduate Admissions for a link to the application and an invitation code to apply for free. The Pitt2Pitt and EAGr applications should be submitted approximately one year prior to your MS starting term and are only available via special invitation code.\nPitt2Pitt\nEAGr\nFuture Terms\nApplicants for all other start terms later than Spring 2028, please share your interest with us below. We will reach out to provide more program information and keep you informed of when the application launches for your term of interest.\nRequest Information\nGraduate\nPrograms & Degrees\nGraduate Programs & Degrees\nOnline Graduate Programs\nCompass Program: Master's Programs for Non-Engineers\nEngineering Accelerated Graduate (EAGr) Program\nGraduate Admissions\nAdmissions Overview\nAdmissions Process\nInternational Graduate Students\nGraduate Application\nApplication Deadlines\nGRE Optional\nTranscripts\nRecommendation Letters\nEnglish Proficiency Scores\nWho's Who\nRecruitment Events\nCompleteU Service\nFunding & Scholarships\nFunding and Scholarships\nPitt2Pitt\nIncoming Students\nGraduate Orientation\nGraduate Housing\nCorporate Partnerships\nContact Us\nEngCAS Applicants\nIf you are having technical difficulties with any part of your application, please contact Engineering CAS customer service via email or at:\nCAS Customer Service\nVirtual Information Sessions\nStay informed and keep up to date with all of our graduate programs and upcoming information sessions and open houses.\nRequest Information\nUpcoming Recruitment Events\nOpen houses, campus events, information sessions and conferences - we're on the road this Fall.\nRecruitment Events\nPreviousNext\nRequest an Application Fee Waiver\nIn an effort to reduce financial barriers to attending graduate school, we offer application fee waivers.\nFee waiver requests are approved on a case-by-case basis as determined by qualifications and financial need. Not all fee waiver requests will be granted. Approval for an application fee waiver is not an offer of admission.\nAs part of this request you'll be asked to include unofficial transcripts from your previous degree(s) and a CV/Resume for review. Please have your materials ready before you begin your request.\nRequest an Application Fee Waiver\nSwanson School of Engineering\nMain Navigation\nApply\nGive\nNews\nAlumni\nVisit\nPick A Path\nCMS Login\nResources\nAbout SSoE\nSSOE Strategic Plan\nConnect\nOpen Positions\nConsumer Information\nNondiscrimination and Anti-Harassment Policy\nPrivacy Policy\nResearch\nAccessibility Statement\nBENEDUM HALL\n3700 O'HARA STREET\nPITTSBURGH, PA 15261\nClose\nStudents\nAcademics\nAdmissions\nAbout Swanson\nResearch\nConnect\nreturn to main menu\nStudents\nGet to Know Us\nCo-op Internships\nGlobal Experiences\nStudent Organizat